  "acrm---key-feature-1-content": "<h3>Follow-up questions on a tick</h3><p>Open a follow-up only when a box is ticked. A client who checks recent surgery is asked what was done and when, and one who checks pregnancy is asked how many weeks along.</p>",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Massage Intake Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a massage intake form?\", \"a\": \"A massage intake form is the questionnaire a client completes before a session, covering contact details, health history, medications, pressure and the areas to work on or avoid. It closes with a signed consent. A massage client intake form tells the therapist what to adjust on the table before anyone starts.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make a massage intake form online?\", \"a\": \"List your questions, then note which answers should open a follow-up or hold a booking. Describe both to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds the form with a client database behind it, and clients fill it on a phone from the booking confirmation.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a massage intake form template include?\", \"a\": \"A massage intake form template starts with contact details and an emergency contact, then health history, medications and allergies to oils or lotions. Pressure preference, a body map and your policies come next. Templates for massage therapy intake forms often treat surgery as a yes or no. Add a line for the date.\"}, {\"q\": \"Why do massage therapists use intake forms?\", \"a\": \"To find out what should change on the table before a session starts. Some conditions need a doctor's clearance before massage, and the form is where a therapist first hears about one. Massage intake forms also record the client's consent to treatment.\"}, {\"q\": \"Are there free massage intake forms?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Professional associations and template galleries post free massage intake forms, mostly as PDFs to print. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing an online version that saves every answer in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should clients fill out a massage intake form?\", \"a\": \"Before the first appointment, as soon as the booking is made. That gives the therapist a day to read the answers and call about anything that needs a conversation first. Clients who walk in can complete it on a tablet at the front desk before they are called through.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a simple massage intake form?\", \"a\": \"It fits on one screen: contact details, a short health check with a follow-up on any yes, pressure, areas to avoid and a signature. A simple massage intake form suits chair massage at events. Pair it with a liability waiver form when the host asks for one.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a therapist do with a massage client intake form?\", \"a\": \"The therapist reads it before the client arrives and adjusts the plan for that session. A recent operation means a phone call before the booking stands. Pressure and areas to avoid carry onto the session sheet, and the signed form stays in the client's record for the next visit.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do regulars need new intake forms for massage therapy?\", \"a\": \"Not the whole form at every visit. Some practices recheck intake forms for massage therapy periodically or once a year. Between those checks, ask regulars at each booking whether anything about their health has changed.\"}, {\"q\": \"What health questions does a massage therapy intake form ask?\", \"a\": \"Expect questions on recent surgery, blood clots, skin conditions and pregnancy, plus medications such as blood thinners. Massage should not be done near a blood clot or a recent incision, which is why a massage therapy intake form asks for dates. Clinics that need a fuller history use a patient intake form.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
  "afb---how-to-step-7-des": "Send the link with the booking confirmation, then fill it once yourself as a test client who ticks every box. Check that each alert lands. On the day itself, read the session sheet at the front desk, before the client is in the room."
 }
}